('09fde0','ActualBank virtual+40 implements local tableC lookup using WORD+156 and DWORD+144, plus bit0x8000 delegation through another bank and bit0x4000 local stripping. The latter branches use signed fallback-to-zero indexes.','The 0x8000 path assumes a driver pointer. A null remote lookup falls back locally without clearing that flag. Other driver virtual implementations and tableC payload semantics are not established.'),
('09fea0','ActualBank virtual+48 selects a sequence index with the signed count+152 comparison. Auxiliary mode returns aux+164*index+32; raw mode returns payload+signedDWORD at the table addressed by DWORD+148.','No selected span, object lifetime, zero-count or negative-index check is supplied here. The128-byte auxiliary record size comes from the separately captured snapshot copy.'),
('09fee0','The duration-like float reader first reads DWORD at aux+164*index+160, otherwise optional sequence section0x2000 +4. Both are zero-extended32-bit values converted via signed64-bit CVTSI2SS and scaled by single-precision0.001. Without that metadata it takes the maximum of zero and the B78F0 values over sequence track references.','Decompiler double/signed-int types are misleading here. The fallback accumulator is signed32-bit while metadata is unsigned32-bit. This is a calculation over descriptors, not proof of audible duration or successful loading.'),
('0a0010','Find-index reduces unsigned input modulo1000 and returns the first sequence whose WORD+12 matches, or UINT32_MAX. Auxiliary entries use164-byte stride. Raw flag0x40 mode optionally obtains backend payload via virtual+56/+8 before search and calls virtual+64 afterward.','The virtual+24 result is dereferenced without a null check. Backend validity/lifetime and semantic completeness of the lock/unlock interface are not established; this is not a safe ID validation entry point.'),
('0a0110','Find-sequence uses the same unsigned modulo1000 first-match search. It returns the auxiliary sequence pointer or the raw virtual+24 pointer; raw flag0x40 processing calls backend virtual+64 before returning the saved pointer.','The returned raw pointer has no new ownership established by this body. Full synchronization and backend virtual contracts are outside the study.'),
('0a0230','Find-auxiliary reduces the key modulo1000, finds a sequence WORD+12, and returns aux+164*index+32 or raw virtual+48(index). Raw flag0x40 processing performs backend virtual+64 before returning.','The32-byte offset is within the compact record, not a serialized file header. Borrowed pointer lifetime and every backend are unresolved.'),
